Feature: Shot-Aware Cross-Cut Consistency for Interactive Placement
  As an editor placing a brand asset in a scene that contains multiple camera cuts
  I want the placement to track and composite correctly in every shot of that scene
  So that the brand asset appears consistently throughout the scene, not just in one camera angle

  Background:
    Given a content item has been processed by ShotDetectionPipeline and ShotClusteringService
    And a SceneItem exists that spans 3 shots, clustered by SAM3 keyframe embedding similarity
    And SAM3 video-rle (fal-ai/sam-3/video-rle) is configured as the tracking engine
    And a SurfaceItem exists with a seed click/quad placed in the scene's first shot

  # ── Surface creation (prerequisite fix) ──

  Scenario: Approving an interactive placement creates a real surface before dispatching a render
    Given I click a product in "Insert Product" mode and receive a SAM3 mask preview
    And I select a brand asset and click "Approve & Render"
    When the editor calls POST /api/surfaces/from-click before POST /api/renders/interactive
    Then a SurfaceItem is persisted with Source="Manual", Status="Approved", and the correct SceneId
    And the render dispatch receives a real surfaceId that resolves successfully

  # ── Shot-aware tracking ──

  Scenario: The seed shot is tracked continuously via a box prompt
    Given the surface's seed frame falls within shot 0 of the scene
    When ShotAwareTrackingService tracks the surface
    Then a single fal-ai/sam-3/video-rle call is made for shot 0's frame range with a box prompt
    And the resulting per-frame masks are stored in TrackingDataJson under shotSegments[0]
    And shotSegments[0].status is "Tracked"

  Scenario: A subsequent shot re-anchors with a text prompt, not the previous shot's coordinates
    Given shot 0 was tracked successfully and shot 1 begins after a hard cut
    When ShotAwareTrackingService processes shot 1
    Then a separate fal-ai/sam-3/video-rle call is made for shot 1's frame range using a text prompt
    And the text prompt is a Gemini-generated visual description of the surface, not shot 0's pixel coordinates
    And shotSegments[1].status is "Reanchored" if a match is found

  Scenario: A shot where the surface cannot be re-detected is skipped, not failed
    Given shot 2 does not contain a visible instance of the surface (occluded or off-screen)
    When ShotAwareTrackingService's text-prompted re-anchor call for shot 2 returns no detection above threshold
    Then shotSegments[2].status is "Skipped" and its frames array is empty
    And the render job passes the source video through unmodified for shot 2's frame range
    And the surface's overall TrackingStatus is "PartialCoverage"
    And the completed render's status is "NeedsReview", not "Failed"

  Scenario: The seed shot itself fails to track
    Given the surface's seed shot has no detection above threshold
    When ShotAwareTrackingService completes
    Then the surface's overall TrackingStatus is "LockLost"
    And the render job throws before compositing anything
    And the render's status is "Failed"

  # ── Planar path ──

  Scenario: A tracked quad is fitted from the RLE mask via min-area-rect, not OpenCV
    Given a tracked frame's RLE mask decodes to a polygon
    When the Planar path processes that frame
    Then MinAreaRectFitter.FitQuad computes a 4-corner quad via rotating calipers
    And no OpenCV dependency is introduced (matches this codebase's ffmpeg-CLI convention)

  Scenario: Planar render reassembles shots into one scene-length clip
    Given shots 0 and 1 were tracked/re-anchored and shot 2 was skipped
    When ProcessPlanarRenderJob composites each shot segment independently
    Then shot 2's frame range is extracted directly from the source video with no compositing
    And VideoChunkingService.SpliceChunksAsync concatenates all three shot outputs in ShotIndex order
    And the final render plays back as one continuous scene-length clip

  # ── Generative path ──

  Scenario: Generative chunking never straddles a shot boundary
    Given the scene's shots have durations of 2s, 6s, and 3s
    When VideoChunkingService.SplitByShotBoundariesAsync splits the scene for pikaswaps
    Then the 2s and 3s shots each become exactly one chunk
    And the 6s shot (exceeding pikaswaps' 4.75s limit) is sub-split only within its own span
    And no chunk boundary falls in the middle of a different shot

  Scenario: Drift-check flags but does not fail a render with weak re-detection confidence
    Given a shot's composited output is re-detected via SAM3 video-rle at its seed frame
    When the re-detected bounding box has IoU < 0.85 against the pre-composite tracked mask
    Then the render completes with status "NeedsReview", not "Failed"
    And the drift IoU is logged for QA review
